comments.content:
Where we pull all of our data from inside `rpc-handler` via `lib/chainlist`
```ts
export async function generateChainData(){
    const chains = await fetcher("https://chainid.network/chains.json");
    const chainTvls = await fetcher("https://api.llama.fi/chains");
    const overwrittenIds = overwrittenChains.reduce((acc, curr)=>{
        acc[curr.chainId] = true;
        return acc
    }, {})
    const sortedChains = chains
      .filter((c) => c.status !== "deprecated" && !overwrittenIds[c.chainId])
      .concat(overwrittenChains)
      .map((chain) => populateChain(chain, chainTvls))
      .sort((a, b) => {
        return (b.tvl ?? 0) - (a.tvl ?? 0);
      });
    return sortedChains
}  
```
https://github.com/ubiquity/rpc-handler/blob/development/build/dynamic-types.ts
We don't perform any actions on the returned data. 
Any suggestions on how we can improve the security and remove that risk from our base of RPCs?
The only things I can think of cost money to run/use idk if there are free services we could use, whitelisting is no good and not scalable.
Is there a platform like chainlist you know of which provides more trusted rpcs?
Sounds like it's actually pretty critical to address this point ASAP if that feature can be hijacked?

